{
    "_about": "What she does when you click on her portrait (3D models). Each zone has a reaction per mood band - cool, neutral, warm, loving, from her warmth, plus lewd and grudge (her rows past the grid; without them she falls back to loving / cool) - and can also name one of her moods (flirty, heated, furious...) to override its band. A reaction: gestures (one is picked at random), face (a quick expression: happy, relaxed, sad, angry, surprised, blush, lids, 0..1), seconds (how long the face holds), emote (hearts, sweat, anger, question), ears (twitch them). Leave a zone out, or a band, and that touch does nothing. Zones: head, nose, mouth, chest, tummy, groin, legs, neck, arms, back, butt, and tail (only on models with tail bones). Gesture files can also join in on their own with touch: ['legs'] and moods: ['warm'] - those are added to a zone's gestures. A reaction can also build up: build is how many touches on that part of her it takes for the full reaction (a number, or { tired, even, wired } by her energy), and soft is what she does until then (a reaction, or one per energy); soft's gesture plays on the first touch only, then just its face. build_seconds: how long a part of her stays warmed up. too_much is what she does when you keep at it. docs/portrait.md explains it all.",
